            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Replace each squared sine by one minus the corresponding squared cosine, then expand and cancel.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Use $\\sin^2\\alpha=1-\\cos^2\\alpha$ and $\\sin^2\\beta=1-\\cos^2\\beta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sin^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha\\sin^2\\beta&=(1-\\cos^2\\alpha)\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha(1-\\cos^2\\beta)\\\\\n\\sin^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha\\sin^2\\beta&=\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha+\\cos^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta\\\\\n\\sin^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha\\sin^2\\beta&=\\cos^2\\beta-\\cos^2\\alpha.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
